<p>LOOKING AHEAD →</p>
<p>Chapter 2 has shown us what the categorical imperative is and how it operates. What Chapter 2 has not done is show us why we are bound by it. Why should you or I care about acting on maxims that can be universalized? Chapter 3 takes up this question, and the answer runs through Kant's account of human freedom.</p>
